# What `project/readme.py`, `project/metadata.py`, `project/docs.py` and `project/run_skill.py` rendered
# before the standing text in them moved out to `assets/`, as SHA-256 over the UTF-8 bytes of each file.
#
# The move is only worth doing if it changed nothing a project receives, and "generate before and after"
# cannot be run across one commit. So these were captured at 074aa35, the commit slice 16.4 was written on
# top of, by the matrix `tests/test_project_pages.py` describes, and the new path has to reproduce them
# exactly. Anyone can take the same reading: check out 074aa35, put that module beside this file, and run
#
#     PYTHONPATH=src:tests python3 -c "import sys, test_project_pages; sys.stdout.write(test_project_pages.lines())"
#
# and compare it with the lines below. The module that prints them changes nothing the generator does, so
# the reading is the same whether it is taken at 074aa35 or at the commit that added it.
#
# Fifty-six combinations: six application sets — a repository the keel made none of, one service, a service
# with a browser app, two services on two rungs with two browser apps, a service with no inbound transport,
# and that service with a browser app beside it — against both profiles and four target-and-shape answers,
# plus the delivery layout for the set whose pages read it.
# `<digest>  <apps>/<profile>/<target>-<shape>/<delivery>  <path>`.
#
# The sixth set was added after the first five were recorded, because it is the only one that reaches the
# run skill's no-transport section and the README's run block with no service to start. Its rows were read
# the same way, at 074aa35 restored from the history — and re-reading the other five there reproduced the
# lines already here byte for byte, which is what makes appending to a record safe rather than a second
# reading of a moved target.
#
# A deliberate edit to one of these pages changes these lines, which is the point: the diff a reviewer has
# to see is the prose, and this file is what refuses to let it pass unseen.
#
# Twenty-four rows moved on 2026-10-12, all of them `skills/run-the-app/SKILL.md` in a combination with a
# browser app. That is not the move changing a byte: it is the fix for a fault the move carried across
# faithfully. Two placeholders in that page, `{web_url}` and `{web_path}`, were written as Python format
# fields in a string that was never an f-string, so a project received them literally — `playwright open
# {web_url}`. Single braces are not the keel's marker either, so the check for a surviving placeholder
# could not see them. They are `{{web-url}}` and `{{web-path}}` now, and `web-path` is a value the page
# may name. Recorded here because a wording change goes in its own commit, never inside a move.
#
# Re-taken for the scheduling rules — two bands, a state per slice, refill at every boundary, a `question`
# deck-log kind (`changelog.d/sail-scheduling-is-a-state.md`). Only the rows named there moved:
# `docs/first-slice.md`. Every other row is still its earlier reading.
#
# Re-taken for a project started from a PRD and for the passphrase row (`changelog.d/generate-lands-in-
# the-project-a-project-starts-from-a-prd.md`, `…-the-readme-says-the-account-keeps-the-passphrase.md`).
# Only the rows named there moved: `README.md` on a managed target, and `docs/skills-and-commands.md`,
# which lists `/draft` and `/launch` now. Every other row is still its earlier reading.
#
# Re-taken for mutation once per capability, bounded (`changelog.d/loop-cadence-mutation-once-per-capability.md`).
# Only the rows named there moved: `docs/workflow.md`. Every other row is still its earlier reading.
# Re-taken for the profile staying put (changelog.d/a-further-feature-stays-on-this-profile.md).
# Only the rows named there moved: docs/intake/README.md. Every other row is still its earlier reading.
#
# Re-taken for clarify, checklist and analyze (`changelog.d/clarify-checklist-and-analyze.md`).
# Only the rows named there moved: `docs/workflow.md`, `docs/intake/README.md`.
# Every other row is still its earlier reading.
# Re-taken 2026-10-17 for changelog.d/capability-gates-once-per-capability.md: the rows for `README.md`, `docs/workflow.md` moved, deliberately — converge, gaps, design review, adversary, mutation and the hand's walk run once per capability, and three of them moved off the slice.
